    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=9$, $b=5$, so $x(t)=\\dfrac{9}{t+1}+5t+1$.\nUse $v(2)=4$ and $\\dfrac{x(2)-x(0)}{2}=2$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}v(t)&=x'(t)=-\\frac{a}{(t+1)^{2}}+b\\\\v(2)&=-\\frac{a}{9}+b=4\\\\\\frac{x(2)-x(0)}{2}&=\\frac{(a/3+2b+1)-(a+1)}{2}=2\\\\b-\\frac{a}{3}&=2\\end{align*}$$\nSubtracting the velocity equation from the average-velocity equation gives\n$$\\begin{align*}-\\frac{2a}{9}&=-2\\\\a&=9\\\\b&=5\\end{align*}$$\nHence $x(t)=\\dfrac{9}{t+1}+5t+1$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
